    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367-a2">

                <pb facs="0591" n="521" xml:id="pg521"/>

                <head>Administration of Foreign Relations and Government–Department of
                    Relations–Section America, number 545.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Durango,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 27, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As I announced to you from Chihuahua on the 9th day of this month, the citizen
                    President of the republic set off from there on the 10th, arriving here
                    yesterday evening.</p>
                <p>Here and in all the towns on the way he was received by the generality of the
                    inhabitants with most patriotic demonstrations of attachment and respect for the
                    first magistrate of the republic and representative of the national cause.</p>
                <p>When the President may determine to go to any other place that may be convenient
                    in view of circumstances, I will promptly communicate to you for your
                    information.</p>
                <p>I assure you of my very respectful consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LERDO DE TEJADA,</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Citizen <hi rendition="#small-caps">Romero,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister
                            Plenipotentiary.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
